  <description promeva:title="Description (English)" promeva:type="104" type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The escalation of the conflict on October 7, 2023, has created a dire need for emergency health and protection (including mental health) programming in Gaza. As of 21:00, 11, Oct, 2023: 1100 fatalities, over 5330 injured and total of 339000 are displaced. This alone necessitates a robust emergency health and protection response. Beyond physical injuries, the conflict is also likely to have a profound impact on the mental well-being of affected individuals. Psychosocial support, counseling, and mental health services are integral to addressing this aspect of the crisis. The severe shortages of essential medications , medical supplies, electricity, and the infrastructure damage, have hampered the functioning of healthcare facilities.  Movement restrictions and security concerns may impede access to healthcare facilities, making it essential to establish mobile clinics and medical teams capable of reaching those in need.</narrative>
  </description>
