  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Health - output</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of live births attended by skilled health personnel</narrative>
    </title>
    <reference code="HEA-I3" indicator-uri="http://www.dutchrelief.org/" vocabulary="99"></reference>
    <baseline value="0" year="2023"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-10-14"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-07-13"></period-end>
     <target value="4200"></target>
     <actual value="1108">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">CARE and PRCS supported a maternity unit at Al-AMAL Hospital in Khan Younis. This support included providing essential medical supplies, such as medications and consumables, as well as non-medical supplies for hospital maintenance.To ensure quality health services for maternity unit beneficiaries, CARE also facilitated incentive payments for the staff throughout the project&apos;s duration. The support provided by CARE to the maternity unit was divided into two main services.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of mental health consultations</narrative>
    </title>
    <reference code="HEA-I2" indicator-uri="http://www.dutchrelief.org/" vocabulary="99"></reference>
    <baseline value="0" year="2023"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-10-14"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-07-13"></period-end>
     <target value="7200"></target>
     <actual value="35992">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">CARE has deployed trained psychosocial workers through PMRS mobile clinics to provide essential mental health services. They primarily target areas with high population densities, such as shelters and UNRWA schools. The PMRS team offered services including psychotherapy, basic management of gender-based violence cases, and referrals for more complex cases to specialized care providers for further intervention.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of children who received community based treatment for malaria, diarrhoea and/or acute respiratory infections</narrative>
    </title>
