  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Accountability - output</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of adaptations in the design and/or implementation of the JR, as a result of the input from beneficiaries</narrative>
    </title>
    <reference code="ACC-I2" indicator-uri="http://www.dutchrelief.org/" vocabulary="99"></reference>
    <baseline value="0" year="2023"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-10-14"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-07-13"></period-end>
     <target value="2"></target>
     <actual value="5">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">due to the rapidly changing situation in Gaza, we made 5 key adaptations to the project activities based on feedback from beneficiaries. These adaptations included changes in the distribution modality, adjustments to project activity locations for security reasons, and shifts in health service delivery from Primary Health Care Centers (PHCC) to mobile medical units where needed, ensuring the project remained responsive to evolving needs on the ground, etc.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of crisis-affected people who are also involved in the design, implementation, monitoring and/or evaluation of the programme</narrative>
    </title>
    <reference code="ACC-I1" indicator-uri="http://www.dutchrelief.org/" vocabulary="99"></reference>
    <baseline value="0" year="2023"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-10-14"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-07-13"></period-end>
     <target value="240"></target>
     <actual value="309">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">thanks to expanded opportunities for engagement in Gaza, particularly during the implementation phase, and the utilization of our feedback channels, we successfully involved 309 people in various activities. This increased participation allowed us to gather valuable input and make necessary adjustments based on their feedback, exceeding our original target.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
